<title>ITALY: Specialists bid for 2.13 trln lire of Italy Cct.</title>
<headline>Specialists bid for 2.13 trln lire of Italy Cct.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Specialist bond traders bid for 2.13 trillion lire of seven-year variable-rate certificates (CCT) against the Italian Treasury's offer of 850 billion lire of paper.</p>
<p>Earlier, the Treasury received bids for 12.65 trillion lire at the open auction for the November 1, 2003 paper, against 8.5 trillion lire worth of certificates on offer.</p>
<p>The auction price was set at 100.35 from 100.95 at the previous CCT sale on December 17.</p>
</text>
